| feature | at rest | grasp anchor ({{anc_scored}} scored, {{anc_fail}} fail) |
|---|---|---|
| our world model | {{rest_W1}} [{{rest_W1_lo}}, {{rest_W1_hi}}] | {{anc_W1}} [{{anc_W1_lo}}, {{anc_W1_hi}}] |
| colour judge (no learning) | {{rest_judge}} [{{rest_judge_lo}}, {{rest_judge_hi}}] | — |
| frozen DINOv2-S | {{rest_W2p}} [{{rest_W2p_lo}}, {{rest_W2p_hi}}] | {{anc_W2p}} [{{anc_W2p_lo}}, {{anc_W2p_hi}}] |
| commanded joints | {{rest_joints}} [{{rest_joints_lo}}, {{rest_joints_hi}}] | {{anc_joints}} [{{anc_joints_lo}}, {{anc_joints_hi}}] |
| policy identity | {{rest_policy}} [{{rest_policy_lo}}, {{rest_policy_hi}}] | — |

![The controls table as a dot plot. Left: AUROC at rest with its 95 % bootstrap CI. Right: AUROC at the grasp anchor, mean of 5 seeds with the seed range (not a CI). Exploratory, LOSO, operator labels.](fig/table2.pdf){#fig:controls}

In this exploratory comparison on the {{n}} rollouts, our world model is level with the colour judge at rest (the CIs overlap) and above the frozen encoder and the joints; at the grasp anchor, where no judge applies, it leads both controls. The anchor column depends on how the seeds are aggregated (exploratory): the AUROC of the 5-seed-averaged predictions is {{anc_W1_avg}} / {{anc_W2p_avg}} / {{anc_joints_avg}} (ours / frozen DINOv2-S / joints), and seed 0 alone gives {{anc_W1_s0}} / {{anc_W2p_s0}} / {{anc_joints_s0}}, a smaller gap between our model and the frozen encoder; the ordering holds in both. The pose probes hold the joints better than our encoder does but the outcome worse, so on these rollouts the encoder holds outcome information they do not (exploratory). The original outcome-readout gate scored our model at {{g10_rest}}, but against the colour judge's labels rather than the operator's, on {{g10_n}} rollouts; the rerun here, on the {{n}} Orin rollouts against operator labels with the controls beside it, gives {{rest_W1}}.

## Where the predictor fails

The cleanest contrast is the grasp probe, which ContactGuard [@zheng2026contactguard] motivates: same encoder, same anchor, current latent {{c1_current}} against imagined latent {{c1_imagined}}, where the bar was {{c1_bar}} over the current latent. On these rollouts, imagining forward loses outcome information the encoder had; this pre-registered row fails, and the encoder/predictor reading built on it stays exploratory. On SURVEYOR's scale check, the frozen DINOv2-S control (τ {{surv_tau_W2p}}) and the joints (τ {{surv_tau_joints}}) pass where our model fails, which points at our model's latent geometry rather than the task.

*Three further exploratory lines.* (1) On the inverse-dynamics term of the distillation probe (pooled, {{g5_val}} teleoperation validation episodes), the trained model ({{g5_w1}}) is not distinguishable from its own random initialisation ({{g5_rand}}): the difference is {{g5_diff}}, with a 95 % paired episode-bootstrap CI of [{{g5_lo}}, {{g5_hi}}] (`gap5_pooled_rerun.json`). The term is sensitive to BLAS and ridge conditioning: the same untrained network scored {{g5_unstable}} on one machine and {{g5_rand}} / {{g5_orin}} on two others. (2) The surprise scorer that gives our model a failure-class AUROC of {{m1_auroc}}, below its sanity bar, reproduces the open-loop corruption ratios at K = 30 (cross-episode {{m1_xep}} vs {{m1_xep_g0}}, constant-first {{m1_cf}} vs {{m1_cf_g0}}; `M1_diag_g0_repro.json`), so that AUROC is a real value and not a load or scorer bug. (3) The predictor of VLA-JEPA is close to action-blind (exploratory, {{m3_n}} anchors; Table @tab:vlajepa): action tokens from another episode change the tokens by {{m3_tok_lo}}–{{m3_tok_hi}} % (relative L2) and the loss by about {{m3_sh}} %; zeroing the tokens changes the loss by about {{m3_zero}} % on average (|Δ| {{m3_zero_lo}}–{{m3_zero_hi}} %), and the forward pass is deterministic. Its failure-class AUROC of {{m3_auroc}}, below the same sanity bar, is therefore a real value, and its table stays unread under the frozen bar.

Table @tab:vlajepa: VLA-JEPA world-model loss at {{m3_n}} anchors with the true action tokens, tokens from another episode (Δ shuffled) and zeroed tokens; the token change is the relative L2 of the shuffled tokens. Exploratory, a spot check, not a power analysis. Source: repro/gaps/expected/M3_diag_action_shuffle.json.

| anchor (episode / frame) | true loss | Δ shuffled (%) | token change (%) | Δ zeroed (%) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| {{m3_0_ep}} / {{m3_0_fr}} | {{m3_0_true}} | {{m3_0_sh}} | {{m3_0_tok}} | {{m3_0_zero}} |
| {{m3_1_ep}} / {{m3_1_fr}} | {{m3_1_true}} | {{m3_1_sh}} | {{m3_1_tok}} | {{m3_1_zero}} |
| {{m3_2_ep}} / {{m3_2_fr}} | {{m3_2_true}} | {{m3_2_sh}} | {{m3_2_tok}} | {{m3_2_zero}} |
